//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @page c_tafsim SIM Service
 *
 * @rst :ref:`API reference <File taf_sim_interface.h>` @endrst
 *
 * <HR>
 *
 * The TelAF Subscriber Identity Module (SIM) service defines APIs related to SIM configuration.
 *
 * SIM is an integrated circuit (IC) intended to securely store the international mobile subscriber
 * identity (IMSI) number and some credentials to identify subscribers. SIM cards can also store a
 * number of SMS messages and phone contacts.
 *
 * @section taf_sim_binding IPC interfaces binding
 *
 * The functions of this service are provided by the @b tafSimCard service.
 *
 * The following example illustrates how to bind to the SIM card service.
 * @verbatim
   bindings:
   {
       clientExe.clientComponent.taf_sim -> tafSimCardSvc.taf_sim
   }
   @endverbatim
 *
 * @section taf_sim_SelectCard Select a card to use
 *
 * taf_sim_SelectCard() is used to select the SIM card available on the user device. By default,
 * the SIM card in slot 1 is used for network camping.
 * Additionally, if the SIM card identifier is passed in any TAF SIM API as a parameter, it will select that
 * SIM and after this taf_sim_GetSelectedCard() will return the newly selected card, not necessarily
 * the one previously set by taf_sim_SelectCard().
 *
 * @b NOTE: The SIM selection is not power off persistent. This function needs to be called at each start-up.
 *
 * @b NOTE: It is highly recommended to wait for a TelAF SIM handler notification after selecting a new SIM
 *          before calling TelAF SIM API functions.
 *
 * @section taf_sim_id SIM identification information
 *
 * \b ICCID:
 * The SIM card is internationally identified by integrated circuit card identifier (ICCID).
 * ICCID is stored in the SIM card and engraved or printed on the body of the SIM card.
 * The ICCID is defined by the ITU-T standard E.118 as the primary account number.
 * According to section E.118, the ICCID is up to 19 digits. It includes a single
 * check digit computed by applying the Luhn algorithm. However, GSM Phase 1 (ETSI
 * Standard GSM 11.11) defined the ICCID length in 10 octets (i.e. 20 digits) with a
 * network-specific structure.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_GetICCID() -- Reads the identification number (ICCID).
 * - @ref taf_sim_AddNewStateHandler() -- Registers a handler to get notification when card state changes.
 * - @ref taf_sim_RemoveNewStateHandler() -- Unregisters the handler.
 *
 * @b NOTE: During the initialization times of service, the new subscriptions of the ICCID change
 *          events are notified by the last changed events. This behavior exists only for 5 seconds and allows
 *          newly registered clients to get any ICCID changes that occured during the device power-on time.
 *
 * \b IMSI:
 * The International Mobile Subscriber Identity (IMSI) is a unique identity associated with
 * the cellular networks. It is used in any mobile network that connects with other networks.
 * The IMSI is provisioned inside the SIM card in case of GSM, UMTS and LTE networks.
 *
 * The IMSI is generally a 15 digits long number, but it can be shorter also. The first 3 digits
 * represent mobile country code (MCC) followed by the mobile network code (MNC), either 2
 * digits (European standard) or 3 digits (North American standard) long. The length of MNC depends
 * on the value of MCC. The remaining digits are the mobile subscription identification number (MSIN)
 * within the operator's customer base.
 *
 * \b EID:
 * The EID (also called as eUICCID) is unique identifier for the embedded Universal Integrated
 * Circuit Card (eUICC).
 * The eUICC is a SIM card having remote provisioning function, and is designed to not be removed or
 * replaced. It enables storing multiple communication profiles but only one is active (recognized
 * by equipment and used for communication with network). With conventional SIM card, the ICCID is
 * a unique key to distinguish the SIM card, but in case of eUICC, the ICCID is useful to identify
 * a profile, and a new identifier is introduced, called eUICCID (EID), which is used as the primary
 * key of the embedded SIM (eSIM) to identify.
 *
 * @ref taf_sim_GetEID() retrieves the EID.
 *
 * <b>International Mobile Subscriber Identity (IMSI)</b>
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_GetIMSI() -- Gets the IMSI.
 *
 * <b>Phone Number</b>
 *
 * @ref taf_sim_GetSubscriberPhoneNumber() -- Reads the phone number of the SIM.
 * If the phone number has not been assigned, it returns the empty string.
 *
 * Using this API gets the subscriber phone number of the SIM.
 *
 * <b>Home Network Information</b>
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_GetHomeNetworkOperator() -- Retrieves the name of the carrier on which this subscription is made.
 * - @ref taf_sim_GetHomeNetworkMccMnc() -- Retrieves the MCC and MNC of the carrier on which this subscription is made.
 *
 * @section taf_sim_auth SIM authentication
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_EnterPIN() -- Enters the Personal Identification Number (PIN) code which
 *   is required before any mobile device functionality can be used.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_GetRemainingPINTries() -- Returns the number of remaining PIN1/PIN2 entry attempts.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_GetRemainingPUKTries() -- Returns the number of remaining PUK retry attempts
 *   left before the SIM get blocked.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_ChangePIN() must be called to change the PIN code.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_Lock() -- Locks the SIM card and enables asking for the PIN1/PIN2 code.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_Unlock() -- Unlocks the SIM card and disables asking for the PIN code.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_Unblock() unblocks the SIM card. If the SIM card is blocked after X unsuccessful
 *   attempts to enter the PIN then @ref taf_sim_Unblock() can be used with Personal Unblocking
 *   (PUK1/PUK2) code to set a new PIN1/PIN2 and unblock the SIM.
 *
 * @section taf_sim_state SIM states
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_IsPresent() -- Indicates whether the SIM is present (and locked) or if it's removed.
 *   Using this API allows client apps to know whether a SIM is present in device's slot.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_IsReady() -- Indicates whether the SIM is ready (PIN code correctly entered
 *   or not required) to use.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_GetState() -- Retrieves the following SIM states.
 *
 *     - @ref TAF_SIM_PRESENT       -- SIM card is present and locked. This is same as TAF_SIM_INSERTED.
 *     - @ref TAF_SIM_ABSENT        -- SIM card is not present, i.e., not inserted.
 *     - @ref TAF_SIM_READY         -- SIM card is present and unlocked.
 *     - @ref TAF_SIM_BLOCKED       -- SIM card is blocked and cannot be used unless it is unlocked it. Not supported.
 *     - @ref TAF_SIM_BUSY          -- SIM card is busy, i.e., it is getting activated, getting unlocked, etc. Not supported.
 *     - @ref TAF_SIM_POWER_DOWN    -- SIM card is powered OFF. Not supported.
 *     - @ref TAF_SIM_STATE_UNKNOWN -- Unknown SIM state; can occur when the state is not determined.
 *     - @ref TAF_SIM_RESTRICTED    -- SIM card is present but not usable due to carrier restrictions.
 *     - @ref TAF_SIM_ERROR         -- SIM card has error; either card is removed or not readable or illegal.
 *
 * A handler function should be registered to receive SIM state notifications.
 * @ref taf_sim_AddNewStateHandler() allows users to register a state change handler.
 *
 * The handler must follow the below prototype:
 * typedef void(*taf_sim_NewStateHandlerFunc_t)(@ref taf_sim_Id_t simId, @ref taf_sim_States_t simState);
 *
 * When the SIM's state change is notified, the handler function is invoked.
 *
 * @b WARNING: If the input *taf_sim_NewStateHandlerFunc_t is null then this function will kill the
 *             calling client.
 *
 * Call @ref taf_sim_GetState() to retrieve the new state of the SIM.
 *
 * @b NOTE: If many applications register handlers for notifications, they
 *          will all receive it.
 *
 * An application may uninstall a state change handler by calling @ref taf_sim_RemoveNewStateHandler().
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_SetPower() -- Powers up or down the specified SIM card.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_Reset() -- Resets the specified SIM card.
 *
 * @b WARNING: The device may need a reboot to detect a SIM insertion or removal. So it is recommended to restart
 *             the device or NAD.
 *
 * Use @ref taf_sim_GetAppTypes() to retrieve application types in the SIM card.
 *
 * @subsection taf_sim_OpenLogicalChannel Logical channels
 *
 * Logical channel is specified by standard ETSI TS 102 221 in the section 8.7. If they are
 * supported by the SIM card, the logical channels allow sending autonomous APDUs on the different
 * channels. In this case the major points are:
 * - The basic channel 0 is available and opened all the time.
 * - The card assigns a number to open a new channel. This channel remains open until
 *   it is closed by the application or until the SIM is deactivated.
 *
 * Use @ref taf_sim_OpenLogicalChannel() or @ref taf_sim_OpenLogicalChannelByAid() to open a logical
 * channel in the SIM card. APDUs then can be sent to SIM card with @ref taf_sim_SendApduOnChannel().
 * When the logical channel is no longer needed, it can be closed using @ref taf_sim_CloseLogicalChannel().
 *
 * Use @ref taf_sim_IsEmergencyCallSubscriptionSelected() to know if the EMERGENCY profile is activated for
 * the specified sim slot.
 *
 * @b WARNING: If no profile is active, it returns LE_NOT_FOUND.
 *
 * Before the SIM sends a message, an application registers a callback handler using taf_sim_AddNewStateHandler().
 * Once the message is sent, the handler will be called indicating the sending status of the message.
 * If the message sending failed, then the handler will be called with the error code.
 *
 * @verbatim
   static void NewSimStateHandler(taf_sim_Id_t simId, taf_sim_States_t simState, void* contextPtr){
       LE_INFO("New SIM event for SIM card: %d SIM state: %d", simId, simState);
       exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);
   }
   taf_sim_NewStateHandlerRef_t msgHandlerRef = taf_sim_AddNewStateHandler(NewSimStateHandler, NULL);
   @endverbatim
 *
 * Applications must use taf_sim_RemoveNewStateHandler() to release @ref taf_sim_NewStateHandlerRef_t
 * message handler reference object when it is no longer used.
 *
 * @section taf_sim_refresh SIM refresh
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_AddRefreshChangeHandler() -- Registers a handler to get notification when SIM refresh state changes.
 * - @ref taf_sim_RemoveRefreshChangeHandler() -- Unregisters the handler.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_CreateSession() -- Creates a refresh session.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_SetRefreshRegisterFiles() -- Sets refresh register files.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_SetRefreshMode() -- Sets refresh mode.
 *
 * - @ref taf_sim_SetRefreshAllow() -- Sets refresh allow or disallow.
 *
 * @section taf_sim_profile_switch SIM profile switch
 *
 * If there are several subscriptions/profiles in the eUICC (multi-profile), and one of
 * them is dedicated to emergency calls (e.g., eCall, ERA-Glonass), local swap is needed to swap as
 * quickly as possible to the emergency profile.
 *
 * "Local swap" means that the user's application must be able to directly request the eUICC to
 * swap to emergency call subscription (ECS).
 *
 * Local swap puts the eUICC in a temporary state, meaning the commercial subscription is replaced
 * by an emergency subscription for a limited time, event triggering the swap back to commercial
 * subscription being controlled by the user's application.
 *
 * The taf_sim_LocalSwapToEmergencyCallSubscription() function requests the multi-profile eUICC to
 * swap to ECS and reboot. The user's application must wait for eUICC reboot to finish and
 * a network connection to be available.
 *
 * The taf_sim_LocalSwapToCommercialSubscription() function requests the multi-profile eUICC to swap
 * back to a commercial subscription and reboot. The user's application must wait for eUICC reboot
 * to finish and a network connection to be available.
 *
 * Unsupported APIs:
 *   -- taf_sim_SetAutomaticSelection()
 *   -- taf_sim_GetAutomaticSelection()
 *
 * <HR>
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * FPLMN list.
 */
REFERENCE FPLMNList;

REFERENCE Refresh;

/**
 * Legacy state support.
 */
DEFINE INSERTED = 0;

/**
 * Legacy slot ID support.
 */
DEFINE EXTERNAL_SLOT_1 = 1;
DEFINE EXTERNAL_SLOT_2 = 2;

/**
 * PIN length.
 */
DEFINE  PIN_MIN_LEN     = (4);
DEFINE  PIN_MAX_LEN     = (8);
DEFINE  PIN_MAX_BYTES   = (PIN_MAX_LEN+1);

/**
 * PUK length.
 */
DEFINE  PUK_MAX_LEN     = (8);
DEFINE  PUK_MAX_BYTES   = (PUK_MAX_LEN+1);
DEFINE  IMSI_LEN    = (15);
DEFINE  IMSI_BYTES  = (IMSI_LEN+1);
/**
 * Maximum number of response bytes for a short APDU as defined by ISO/IEC 7816-4.
 * Includes 256 bytes for the maximum length of the response data field in a short APDU,
 * plus 2 bytes for the response trailer, status words SW1 and SW2.
 */
DEFINE  RESPONSE_MAX_BYTES  = (256+2);
/**
 * Maximum number of command bytes for a short APDU as defined by ISO/IEC 7816-4.
 * Includes 1 byte each for CLA, INS, P1, and P2,
 * 1 byte for Lc, up to 255 bytes for the data field, and 1 byte for Le.
 */
DEFINE  APDU_MAX_BYTES  = (255+6);
DEFINE  PHONE_NUM_MAX_LEN   = (15+2);
DEFINE  PHONE_NUM_MAX_BYTES = (PHONE_NUM_MAX_LEN+1);

DEFINE  ICCID_LEN    = (20);
DEFINE  ICCID_BYTES  = (ICCID_LEN+1);

DEFINE  EID_LEN    = (32);
DEFINE  EID_BYTES  = (EID_LEN+1);
DEFINE  FILE_ID_LEN  = (4);
DEFINE  FILE_ID_BYTES  = (FILE_ID_LEN+1);
DEFINE  PATH_MAX_LEN  = (100);
DEFINE  PATH_MAX_BYTES  = (PATH_MAX_LEN+1);

DEFINE AID_MAX_LEN = (4);

DEFINE  AID_LEN    = (32);
DEFINE  AID_BYTES  = (AID_LEN+1);

DEFINE MAX_APP_TYPE = (5);

DEFINE FPLMN_MAX_LISTS = (1);
DEFINE FPLMN_MAX_OPERATORS_PER_LIST = (5);

DEFINE MAX_SIM_PATH = 10;
DEFINE MAX_SIM_REFRESH_FILES = 100;

/**
 * Defines SIM card states.
 */
ENUM States
{
    PRESENT,                   ///< SIM card is present and locked. This is same as TAF_SIM_INSERTED.
    ABSENT,                    ///< SIM card is absent.
    READY,                     ///< SIM card is present and ready to use.
    BLOCKED,                   ///< SIM card is blocked and cannot be used unless it is unlocked. Not supported.
    BUSY,                      ///< SIM card is busy, i.e., it is getting activated, getting unlocked, etc. Not supported.
    POWER_DOWN,                ///< SIM card is powered OFF. Currently this is not supported.
    STATE_UNKNOWN,             ///< SIM card state is unknown.
    RESTRICTED,                ///< SIM card is present but not usable due to carrier restrictions.
    ERROR                      ///< SIM card has error; either card is removed or not readable or illegal.
};

/**
 * Defines slot ID of the SIM card.
 */
ENUM Id
{
    EMBEDDED,           ///< Not supported
    SLOT_ID_1,          ///< SIM inserted in slot 1.
    SLOT_ID_2,          ///< SIM inserted in slot 2.
    REMOTE,             ///< Not supported.
    UNSPECIFIED,        ///< Slot ID is unspecified; use the current selected slot ID.
    ID_MAX
};

/**
 * Defines all types of card locks using in PIN management APIs.
 */
ENUM LockType
{
   PIN1 = 0,        ///< Lock type is PIN1.
   PIN2 = 1,        ///< Lock type is PIN2.
   PUK1 = 2,        ///< Lock type is PIN Unblocking Key 1.
   PUK2 = 3,        ///< Lock type is PIN Unblocking Key 2.
   FDN  = 4         ///< Lock type is Fixed Dialing number.
};

ENUM LockResponse
{
    CHANGE_PIN,        ///< Change PIN.
    UNLOCK_BY_PIN,     ///< Unlock PIN.
    UNLOCK_BY_PUK,     ///< Unlock PUK.
    SET_LOCK           ///< Set lock.
};

/**
 * Defines all types of UICC applications, such as SIM, RUIM, USIM, CSIM and ISIM.
 */
ENUM AppType {
   APPTYPE_UNKNOWN = 0, ///< Unknown application type.
   APPTYPE_SIM = 1,     ///< UICC application type is SIM.
   APPTYPE_USIM = 2,    ///< UICC application type is USIM.
   APPTYPE_RUIM = 3,    ///< UICC application type is RSIM.
   APPTYPE_CSIM = 4,    ///< UICC application type is CSIM.
   APPTYPE_ISIM = 5,    ///< UICC application type is ISIM.
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Card manufacturer.
 *
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM Manufacturer
{
    OBERTHUR,           ///< Oberthur.
    GEMALTO,            ///< Gemalto.
    G_AND_D,            ///< G&D.
    MORPHO,             ///< Morpho. Not supported.
    VALID,              ///< Valid. Not supported.
    IDEMIA,             ///< Idemia.
    MANUFACTURER_MAX    ///< Indicates the last item.
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * SIM commands. Refer to TS 11.11 9.1.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM Command
{
    READ_BINARY = 0xb0,            ///< Reads a transparent elementary file.
    READ_RECORD = 0xb2,            ///< Reads a file record.
    GET_RESPONSE = 0xc0,           ///< Gets response.
    UPDATE_BINARY = 0xd6,          ///< Updates a transparent elementary file.
    UPDATE_RECORD = 0xdc,          ///< Updates a file record.
    COMMAND_MAX                    ///< Indicates the last item.
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * SIM refresh session type.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM SessionType
{
    SESSION_TYPE_PRI_GW_PROV = 0,
    SESSION_TYPE_SEC_GW_PROV = 1
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * SIM refresh mode.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BITMASK RefreshMode
{

    REFRESH_MODE_RESET,
    REFRESH_MODE_INIT,
    REFRESH_MODE_INIT_FCN,
    REFRESH_MODE_FCN,
    REFRESH_MODE_INIT_FULL_FCN,
    REFRESH_MODE_APP_RESET,
    REFRESH_MODE_3G_RESET
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * SIM refresh stage.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BITMASK RefreshStatus
{
    REFRESH_STATUS_SUCCESS,
    REFRESH_STATUS_FAILURE,
    REFRESH_STATUS_FILE_CHANGE,
    REFRESH_STATUS_PROFILE_SWITCH
};

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * SIM refresh register files.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRUCT RefreshRegFile
{
    uint16 file_id;
    string path[MAX_SIM_PATH];
};

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Handler for SIM refresh changes.
 *
 * @param[in] refreshStatus SIM refresh status.
 * @param[in] contextPtr    Context pointer.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HANDLER RefreshChangeHandler
(
    RefreshStatus refreshStatus IN      ///< SIM refresh status.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * SIM refresh state change event.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EVENT RefreshChange
(
    RefreshChangeHandler handler    ///< Refresh change handler.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Creates refresh session.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_FAULT            Failed.
 * - LE_OK               Succeeded.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CreateSession
(
    SessionType sessionType     IN,  ///< Session type.
    Refresh refreshSessionRef   OUT  ///< Refresh session reference.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Sets the files to be registered for the refresh notifications.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_FAULT            Failed.
 * - LE_OK               Succeeded.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetRefreshRegisterFiles
(
    Refresh refreshSessionRef      IN,                  ///< Refresh session reference.
    RefreshRegFile files[MAX_SIM_REFRESH_FILES] IN     ///< Files to be registered for the refresh notifications.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Sets refresh mode.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_FAULT            Failed.
 * - LE_OK               Succeeded.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetRefreshMode
(
    Refresh refreshSessionRef      IN,  ///< Refresh session reference.
    RefreshMode refreshMode        IN   ///< Refresh mode.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Sets refresh allow or disallow.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_FAULT            Failed.
 * - LE_OK               Succeeded.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetRefreshAllow
(
    Refresh refreshSessionRef     IN,  ///< Refresh session reference.
    bool isRefreshAllowed         IN   ///< Refresh allow or disallow flag.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Handler for SIM card state changes.
 *
 * @param[in] slotId     Slot ID.
 * @param[in] state      SIM card state.
 * @param[in] contextPtr Context pointer.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HANDLER NewStateHandler
(
    Id       slotId IN,    ///< Slot ID.
    States   state IN      ///< SIM card state.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * SIM card state change event.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EVENT NewState
(
    NewStateHandler handler    ///< State change handler.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Handler for PIN1/PIN2/PUK1/PUK2 changes.
 *
 * @param[in] slotId       The SIM identifier.
 * @param[in] responsetype Lock response type.
 * @param[in] result       Result.
 * @param[in] contextPtr   Context pointer.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HANDLER AuthenticationResponseHandler
(
    Id             slotId IN,             ///< The SIM identifier.
    LockResponse   responsetype IN,       ///< Lock response type.
    le_result_t    result IN              ///< Result.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Authentication response.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EVENT AuthenticationResponse
(
    AuthenticationResponseHandler handler    ///< Authentication response handler.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Checks whether SIM card is present or absent.
 *
 * @return
 * - True -- SIM card present.
 * - False -- SIM card absent.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION bool IsPresent
(
    Id      slotId IN    ///< Slot ID.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Gets the state of the SIM card for the given slotId.
 *
 * @return Current of SIM card state.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION States GetState
(
    Id slotId IN    ///< Slot ID.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Checks whether the SIM card is ready or not
 *
 * @return
 * - True -- SIM card is present and ready to use, i.e., unlocked.
 * - False -- SIM card is absent or restricted to use, i.e., locked.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION bool IsReady
(
    Id slotId IN    ///< Slot ID.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Retrieves the SIM's ICCID.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OK                  ICCID was read successfully.
 * - LE_OVERFLOW            Buffer size is too small.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER       Invalid parameters.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND           Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetICCID
(
    Id        slotId IN,                 ///< Slot ID.
    string    iccid[ICCID_LEN] OUT       ///< ICC ID as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Retrieves the IMSI for the SIM.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OVERFLOW         Buffer size is too small.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER    Invalid parameters.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND        Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_OK               IMSI retrieved successfully.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetIMSI
(
    Id        slotId IN,             ///< Slot ID.
    string    imsi[IMSI_LEN] OUT     ///< IMSI as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Retrieves the name of the carrier on which this subscription is made.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OVERFLOW         Buffer size is too small.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND        Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER    Invalid parameters.
 * - LE_OK               Carrier name retrieved successfully.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetHomeNetworkOperator
(
    Id        slotId IN,             ///< Slot ID.
    string    nameStr[100] OUT       ///< Network name as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Retrieves the phone number for the SIM subscription.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OVERFLOW         Buffer size is too small.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER    Invalid parameters.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND        Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_OK               Phone number retrieved successfully.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetSubscriberPhoneNumber
(
    Id        slotId IN,                                ///< Slot ID.
    string    phoneNumberStr[PHONE_NUM_MAX_LEN] OUT     ///< Phone number as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Retrieves the MNC and MCC of the carrier to which the phone is connected.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OVERFLOW         Buffer size is too small.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND        Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER    Invalid parameters.
 * - LE_OK               Phone number retrieved successfully.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetHomeNetworkMccMnc
(
    Id     slotId IN,        ///< Slot ID.
    string mccPtr[3] OUT,    ///< 3 digit numeric MCC string as output.
    string mncPtr[3] OUT     ///< 2 or 3 digit numeric MNC string as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Gets the slotId of currently selected SIM card.
 *
 * @return slotId of currently selected card.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION Id GetSelectedCard
(
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Selects a SIM.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_FAULT            Failed to select SIM card.
 * - LE_OK               SIM card selected successfully.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SelectCard
(
    Id    slotId IN    ///< Slot ID.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Unlocks the Sim card for an app by entering PIN1/PIN2.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER   Invalid parameters.
 * - LE_UNDERFLOW       PIN code length is too short (minimum 4 digits).
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND       Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_FAULT           Failed to send unlock SIM card by PIN request.
 * - LE_OK              Successfully sent unlock SIM by password request.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t EnterPIN
(
    Id        slotId IN,           ///< Slot ID of SIM.
    LockType  lockType IN,         ///< Applicable lock types are PIN1/PIN2.
    string    pin[PIN_MAX_LEN] IN  ///< PIN1/PIN2.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Changes the PIN1/PIN2.
 *
 * @return LE_BAD_PARAMETER   Invalid SIM slot ID.
 * @return LE_UNDERFLOW       PIN code length is too short (minimum 4 digits).
 * @return LE_NOT_FOUND       Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * @return LE_FAULT           Failed to send change password for lock SIM card request.
 * @return LE_OK              Successfully sent change SIM lock password request.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ChangePIN
(
    Id        slotId IN,                  ///< Slot ID of SIM.
    LockType  lockType IN,                ///< Applicable lock types are PIN1 and PIN2.
    string    oldpin[PIN_MAX_LEN] IN,     ///< Old PIN1/PIN2.
    string    newpin[PIN_MAX_LEN] IN      ///< New PIN1/PIN2.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Gets the number of remaining PIN1 or PIN2 tries.
 *
 * @return
 * - A negative value           Failed to get the number of remaining PIN insertion tries.
 * - Zero or a positive value   Successfully retrieved the retry count value.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION int32 GetRemainingPINTries
(
    Id      slotId IN        ///< Slot ID.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Gets the number of remaining PUK tries.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER   Invalid SIM slot ID.
 * - LE_OK              Successfully get the number of remaining PUK insertion tries.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetRemainingPUKTries
(
    Id      slotId                 IN,    ///< Slot ID.
    uint32  remainingPukTriesPtr  OUT     ///< Number of PUK retries remaining.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Unlocks the SIM card and disables the lock request of PIN1/PIN2.
 *
 * @return LE_BAD_PARAMETER   Invalid SIM slot ID.
 * @return LE_UNDERFLOW       PIN code length is too short (minimum 4 digits).
 * @return LE_NOT_FOUND       Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * @return LE_FAULT           Failed to send disable lock SIM card request.
 * @return LE_OK              Successfully sent disable SIM lock request.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t Unlock
(
    Id        slotId IN,           ///< Slot ID of SIM.
    LockType  lockType IN,         ///< Applicable lock types are PIN1/PIN2.
    string    pin[PIN_MAX_LEN] IN  ///< PIN1/PIN2.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Locks the SIM card and enables the lock request of PIN1/PIN2.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER   Invalid SIM slot ID.
 * - LE_UNDERFLOW       PIN code length is too short (minimum 4 digits).
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND       Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_FAULT           Failed to send enable lock SIM card request.
 * - LE_OK              Successfully sent the enable SIM lock request.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t Lock
(
    Id        slotId IN,           ///< Slot ID of SIM.
    LockType  lockType IN,         ///< Applicable lock types are PIN1/PIN2.
    string    pin[PIN_MAX_LEN] IN  ///< PIN1/PIN2.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Unblocks the SIM card by entering PUK1/PUK2 and new PIN1/PIN2.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER   Invalid SIM slot ID.
 * - LE_OUT_OF_RANGE    PUK length is not correct (8 digits).
 * - LE_UNDERFLOW       PIN code length is too short (minimum 4 digits).
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND       Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_FAULT           Failed to send unlock SIM card request.
 * - LE_OK              Successfully sent the unlock SIM request.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t Unblock
(
    Id        slotId IN,              ///< Slot ID of SIM.
    LockType  lockType IN,            ///< Applicable lock types are PUK1/PUK2.
    string    puk[PUK_MAX_LEN] IN,    ///< PUK1/PUK2.
    string    newpin[PIN_MAX_LEN] IN  ///< New PIN1/PIN2.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Requests eUICC identifier(EID) for the slot.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER    Invalid SIM slot ID.
 * - LE_OVERFLOW         Buffer size is too small.
 * - LE_FAULT            Failed.
 * - LE_OK               Succeeded.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetEID
(
    Id       slotId IN,            ///< Slot ID.
    string   eid[EID_LEN] OUT      ///< eID
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Enables or disables the automatic SIM selection.
 * @b NOTE: Currently this API is not supported.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OK       Succeeded.
 * - LE_FAULT    Failed.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetAutomaticSelection
(
    bool enable IN      ///< Enable flag
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Gets the automatic SIM selection.
 * @b NOTE: Currently this API is not supported.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OK       Succeeded.
 * - LE_FAULT    Failed.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetAutomaticSelection
(
    bool enable OUT        ///< Enable flag as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Gets the application types of a SIM.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OK             Successfully get types of card applications.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER  Invalid parameter.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND      Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_FAULT          Failed to get types of card applications.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetAppTypes
(
     Id slotId IN,                         ///< Slot ID.
     AppType apptype[MAX_APP_TYPE] OUT     ///< Application type.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Opens a logical channel to the SIM.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OK             Successfully opened logical channel request.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER  Invalid parameter.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND      Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_FAULT          Failed to open logical channel.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t OpenLogicalChannel
(
     Id slotId IN,           ///< Slot ID.
     AppType apptype IN,     ///< App type.
     uint8 channelPtr OUT    ///< Channel as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Opens a logical channel by AID input to the SIM.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OK             Successfully opened logical channel request.
 * - LE_OVERFLOW       Buffer size is too small.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER  Invalid parameter.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND      Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_FAULT          Failed to open logical channel.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t OpenLogicalChannelByAid
(
     Id slotId IN,                  ///< Slot ID.
     string aid[AID_BYTES] IN,      ///< Application identifier (AID)
     uint8 channelPtr OUT           ///< Channel as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Closes a previously opened logical channel to the SIM.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OK             Successfully closed the logical channel.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER  Invalid parameter.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND      Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_FAULT          Failed to send the request.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t CloseLogicalChannel
(
    Id    slotId IN,      ///< Slot ID.
    uint8 channel IN      ///< The channel ID to be closed.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Transmits an APDU to the ICC card over a logical channel.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OK             Succeeded.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER  Invalid parameter.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND      Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_FAULT          Failed to transmit APDU.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SendApduOnChannel
(
    Id           simId IN,                                ///< Slot ID.
    uint8        channel IN,                              ///< Channel.
    uint8        commandApdu[APDU_MAX_BYTES] IN,          ///< APDU.
    uint8        responseApdu[RESPONSE_MAX_BYTES] OUT     ///< Response of APDU as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Exchanges APDUs with the SIM on a basic channel.
 *
 * @return
 * - LE_OK             Succeeded.
 * - LE_FAULT          Failed to transmit APDU.
 * - LE_NOT_FOUND      Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 * - LE_BAD_PARAMETER  Invalid parameter.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SendApdu
(
    Id           simId IN,                                 ///< Slot ID.
    uint8        commandApdu[APDU_MAX_BYTES] IN,           ///< APDU command.
    uint8        responseApdu[RESPONSE_MAX_BYTES] OUT      ///< Response of APDU as output.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Sends a command to the SIM.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK             Succeeded.
 *      - LE_FAULT          Failed.
 *      - LE_BAD_PARAMETER  A parameter is invalid.
 *      - LE_NOT_FOUND      Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SendCommand
(
    Id             simId IN,                                ///< The SIM identifier.
    Command        command IN,                              ///< The SIM command.
    string         fileIdentifier[FILE_ID_LEN] IN,          ///< The file identifier.
    uint8          p1 IN,                                   ///< Parameter P1 passed to the SIM.
    uint8          p2 IN,                                   ///< Parameter P2 passed to the SIM.
    uint8          p3 IN,                                   ///< Parameter P3 passed to the SIM.
    uint8          data[APDU_MAX_BYTES] IN,                 ///< The command data.
    string         path[PATH_MAX_LEN] IN,                   ///< The path to the elementary file.
    uint8          sw1 OUT,                                 ///< Status word 1 received from the SIM.
    uint8          sw2 OUT,                                 ///< Status word 2 received from the SIM.
    uint8          response[RESPONSE_MAX_BYTES] OUT         ///< SIM response.
);

/**
 * Switches the given SIM to the emergency call subscription.
 * The eUICC reboots after switching the profile and the client app must wait for it.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_BAD_PARAMETER -- Invalid parameters.
 *      - LE_UNSUPPORTED -- Not supported. This API is not supported for manufacturer MORPHO and VALID.
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Unexpected error.
 *
 * @b NOTE: The eUICC should be in the Ready state.
 *
 * @b NOTE: Ensure the emergency profile is available on the eUICC or an error will be thrown.
 *
 * @b NOTE: This API is not supported for manufacturer MORPHO and VALID.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t LocalSwapToEmergencyCallSubscription
(
    Id           simId IN,                ///< The SIM identifier.
    Manufacturer manufacturer IN          ///< The card manufacturer.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Switches the given SIM to the commercial subscription.
 * The eUICC reboots after switching the profile and the client app must wait for it.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_BAD_PARAMETER -- Invalid parameters.
 *      - LE_UNSUPPORTED -- Not supported.
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Unexpected error.
 *
 * @b NOTE: The eUICC should be in the Ready state.
 *
 * @b NOTE: Ensure the commercial profile is available on the eUICC or an error will be thrown.
 *
 * @b NOTE: This API is not supported for manufacturer MORPHO and VALID.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t LocalSwapToCommercialSubscription
(
    Id           simId IN,                ///< The SIM identifier.
    Manufacturer manufacturer IN          ///< The card manufacturer.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Powers up or down the SIM.
 *
 * @return
 *     - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *     - LE_FAULT -- Failed.
 *     - LE_NOT_FOUND  -- Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 *     - LE_BAD_PARAMETER -- Incorrect parameter(s).
 *
 * @b NOTE: For Multiple SIM power cycle (ON/OFF) operations, it must wait until completing the
 * previous SIM power cycle operation (if any).
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetPower
(
    Id           simId IN,                  ///< The SIM identifier.
    le_onoff_t   power IN                   ///< The power state.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Reset the SIM.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Failed.
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t Reset
(
    Id simId IN                          ///< The SIM identifier.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Checks if the emergency profile is activated for the SIM slot.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK -- Succeeded.
 *      - LE_BAD_PARAMETER -- Invalid SIM identifier or null ECS pointer.
 *      - LE_NOT_FOUND -- Wrong SIM card to operate on.
 *      - LE_FAULT -- Unexpected error.
 *
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t IsEmergencyCallSubscriptionSelected
(
    Id    simId IN,  ///< The SIM identifier.
    bool  isEcs OUT  ///< - True -- Emergency call subscription (ECS) is selected.
                     ///< - False -- Commercial subscription is selected.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Handler for ICCID change events.
 *
 * @param[in] simId      The SIM identifier.
 * @param[in] iccid      ICCID.
 * @param[in] contextPtr Context pointer.
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HANDLER IccidChangeHandler
(
    Id       simId IN,               ///< The SIM identifier.
    string   iccid[ICCID_LEN] IN     ///< ICCID.
);

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * ICCID information.
 *
 */
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EVENT IccidChange
(
    IccidChangeHandler handler
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Creates an empty FPLMN list to insert the FPLMN operators.
 *
 * @return
 *      - Reference to the list object.
 *      - Null pointer if not able to create list reference.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION FPLMNList CreateFPLMNList
(
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Adds the FPLMN network into the newly created FPLMN list.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_FAULT         Failed.
 *      - LE_OK            Succeeded.
 *      - LE_OVERFLOW      The FPLMN operator cannot be inserted into the FPLMN list.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t AddFPLMNOperator
(
    FPLMNList fplmnListRef IN,                    ///< FPLMN list reference.
    string    mcc[3]       IN,                    ///< 3 digit numeric code representing Mobile Country Code.
    string    mnc[3]       IN                     ///< 2 or 3 digit numeric code representing Mobile Network Code.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Reads the first FPLMN network from the list of FPLMN objects retrieved with
 * taf_sim_ReadFPLMNList().
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_FAULT         Failed.
 *      - LE_OK            Succeeded.
 *      - LE_OVERFLOW      MCC/MNC string size is greater than the string length parameter that has
 *                         been given to this function.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetFirstFPLMNOperator
(
    FPLMNList fplmnListRef IN,               ///< FPLMN list reference.
    string mccPtr[3] OUT,                    ///< 3 digit numeric MCC string as output.
    string mncPtr[3] OUT                     ///< 2 or 3 digit numeric MNC string as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Reads the next FPLMN network from the list of FPLMN objects retrieved with taf_sim_ReadFPLMNList().
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_FAULT         Failed.
 *      - LE_OK            Succeeded.
 *      - LE_OVERFLOW      MCC/MNC string size is greater than string length parameter that has
 *                         been given to this function.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetNextFPLMNOperator
(
    FPLMNList fplmnListRef IN,               ///< FPLMN list reference.
    string mccPtr[3] OUT,                    ///< 3 digit numeric code MCC as output.
    string mncPtr[3] OUT                     ///< 2 or 3 digit numeric code MNC as output.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Reads the FPLMN list from the SIM.
 *
 * @return
 *      - Reference to the list object.
 *      - Null pointer if the FPLMN list is not able to read from the SIM.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION FPLMNList ReadFPLMNList
(
    Id       simId IN                       ///< SIM identifier.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Deletes the FPLMN list created by taf_sim_ReadFPLMNList() or taf_sim_CreateFPLMNList().
 *
 * @b NOTE:
 *      On failure, the process exits so that users do not have to worry about checking the returned
 *      reference for validity.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION DeleteFPLMNList
(
    FPLMNList fplmnListRef IN               ///< FPLMN list reference.
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Writes the FPLMN list into the SIM.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_FAULT         Failed.
 *      - LE_OK            Succeeded.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t WriteFPLMNList
(
    Id        simId IN,                     ///< SIM identifier.
    FPLMNList fplmnListRef IN               ///< FPLMN list reference.
);

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Gets the SIM slot count.
 *
 * @return LE_FAULT            Failed to retrieve the slot count.
 * @return LE_OK               The slot count was retrieved successfully.
 *
 */
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetSlotCount
(
    int32     count OUT        ///< Slot count.
);
